{
  "id": "06348_miwakeru",
  "headword": "{見分|みわ}ける",
  "reading": "みわける",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to distinguish; to tell apart",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{見分|みわ}け"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to distinguish; to tell apart; to differentiate",
      "explanation": "To recognize the difference between similar things or people by looking at them."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06348_miwakeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{双子|ふたご}を{見分|みわ}けるのは{難|むずか}しい。",
      "english": "It's hard to tell twins apart.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06348_miwakeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{本物|ほんもの}と{偽物|にせもの}を{見分|みわ}ける{方法|ほうほう}を{教|おし}えてください。",
      "english": "Please teach me how to distinguish the real from the fake.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06348_miwakeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{新鮮|しんせん}な{魚|さかな}と{古|ふる}い{魚|さかな}を{見分|みわ}けられますか。",
      "english": "Can you tell fresh fish from old fish?",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Takes を. Compound verb: {見|み}る + {分|わ}ける.\n\nNUANCE: Emphasizes visual discrimination - the ability to see and recognize differences. Compare with {聞|き}き{分|わ}ける (to distinguish by hearing).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・AとBを{見分|みわ}ける: to tell A and B apart\n・{見分|みわ}けがつかない: to be indistinguishable\n・{見分|みわ}けられる: to be able to distinguish\n\nSIMILAR:\n・{区別|くべつ}する: to distinguish, to differentiate (more general)\n・{判別|はんべつ}する: to discriminate, to identify (more formal)",
  "cross_references": [
